---
/**
 * PieceArt — the die-cut jigsaw slab behind a card's content.
 *
 * Pure structure, no geometry: three extrusion layers, each a body box
 * plus two joint tiles. ALL the shape lives in global.css as two data-URI
 * tiles (--joint-lr, --joint-tb) that serve both as the knob fill (masked
 * spans) and as the socket cut (mask-composite on the bodies) — so a knob
 * and its socket are the same shape BY CONSTRUCTION and the pieces must
 * fit (see the placement rule in global.css). All vector, no filters: the
 * old masked filter stack rasterised and blurred under the grid's
 * transform — that was both the pixelation and the lag.
 *
 * Three layers, back to front (the grid tilts on one axis, so the bottom
 * edge is the only side we see):
 *   piece-shadow — the cast shadow, below only;
 *   piece-wall   — the slab's side wall below the face;
 *   piece-face   — the flat face, sockets cut through every layer.
 */
---

<span class="piece piece-base" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="piece-shadow">
    <span class="piece-body"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-r"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-b"></span>
  </span>
  <span class="piece-wall">
    <span class="piece-body"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-r"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-b"></span>
  </span>
  <span class="piece-face">
    <span class="piece-body"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-r"></span>
    <span class="joint joint-b"></span>
  </span>
</span>
